# muster route golden — every route RegisterRoutes registers, sorted.
#
# Generated by: UPDATE_ROUTES_GOLDEN=1 go test ./internal/api -run TestRoutesMatchGolden
# then READ the diff in `git diff` before committing it.
#
# Patterns only. This file does NOT record auth wrappers — see the KNOWN LIMIT
# banner in routes_golden_test.go before treating a clean diff here as evidence
# that a route's authorisation tier has not changed. It is not.
#
# 🔴 THIS HEADER USED TO SAY THE FILE WAS DELIBERATELY EMPTY BECAUSE "muster has
# no HTTP server yet". THAT BECAME FALSE WHEN THE HTTP LAYER LANDED, and the
# stale sentence is worth REPLACING rather than deleting: a reader who believed
# it would read a diff that ADDS routes as a diff that should not exist, which is
# the reverse of what this gate is for.
#
# The server is here. RegisterRoutes calls (&Server{}).registerAll(mux), and the
# lines below are what it registers. The gate's positive control is the ordinary
# one now: the recorded set must equal this file, and the set is recorded from a
# ZERO-VALUE Server — which is what TestRegistrationIsIndependentOfDependencies
# exists to keep honest, so this file can never become a record of the EMPTY
# configuration while production registers more.
#
# ⚠ A CLI ALSO READS THIS FILE. cmd/muster's TestEveryWiredRouteIsServedByThisProject
# runs every verb, observes the routes that reach the wire, and demands each be
# listed here — the check that keeps its single base URL sufficient. So a route
# DELETED from this file is not only a server change; it can make a client verb
# unreachable, and that test is where it surfaces.
